<title>USA: Fewer than half of NY banks borrowed March 19 wk.</title>
<headline>Fewer than half of NY banks borrowed March 19 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fewer than half of the six major New York City banks borrowed from the Federal Reserve's discount window in the March 19 week, a Fed spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>This is the first time borrowing was done since the week ended January 15, 1997. No further details were available.</p>
<p>It was the middle of the two-week bank maintenance period.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
